# EXPERIMENT (branch experiment/cmu-motion-space): faithful multi-node CMU gait graph.
# Built data-driven from the full 10x10 transition-distance sweep (out/transition_matrix.txt).
#
# Topology is 2 nodes, NOT 3, because the sweep shows a hard WALL between walk and
# the jog/run cluster (every walk<->fast crossing D>=998), while jog<->run is cheap
# (16_35->16_45 D=67, 16_36->16_45 D=270). So jog sits WITH run on the far side of
# the wall -- one "run" node spanning ~47-70 cm/s -- and walk is its own node.
#
# Node clips chosen for low loop-seam + clean within-node transition:
#   walk_cmu: 16_31 @17.1, 16_21 @29.9  (within-D 15/79, seams 0.065/0.050)
#   run_cmu : 16_36 @47.1, 16_45 @69.9  (within-D 270/893, seams 0.179/0.307)
# Edge thresholds are native cm^2 from the sweep. The ~6x gap between self-edges
# (~250/950) and cross-edges (~1350/1550) IS the measured cost of a gait change with
# NO transition clip in the corpus (paper sec.6 limitation): the graph connects, but
# the walk<->run edges are the reliability bottleneck, not a clean planted transition.

node walk_cmu 1
registration walk_cmu LeftFoot - 3 0
parameter_metrics walk_cmu travel_speed
parameter_calibration walk_cmu 9
parameter_support walk_cmu simplex
example walk_cmu 17.1 bvh/16_31.bvh start_frame 290 end_frame 419
example walk_cmu 29.9 bvh/16_21.bvh start_frame 10 end_frame 129

node run_cmu 1
registration run_cmu LeftFoot - 3 0
parameter_metrics run_cmu travel_speed
parameter_calibration run_cmu 9
parameter_support run_cmu simplex
example run_cmu 47.1 bvh/16_36.bvh start_frame 45 end_frame 139
example run_cmu 69.9 bvh/16_45.bvh start_frame 5 end_frame 89

expect walk_cmu spanned_axes 1
expect run_cmu spanned_axes 1

edge walk_cmu walk_cmu
edge_phase_range walk_cmu walk_cmu 0.70 0.95 0.05 0.30
edge_config walk_cmu walk_cmu 250 450 4 6 41

edge run_cmu run_cmu
edge_phase_range run_cmu run_cmu 0.70 0.95 0.05 0.30
edge_config run_cmu run_cmu 950 1300 4 6 41

# CROSS-GAIT edges (the wall). In the build's kovar point-cloud metric the BEST
# achievable crossing is D~2709 (walk->run) / D~1932 (run->walk) at EVERY source
# sample -- ~10x the within-gait self-edge (~250). No GOOD transition exists because
# subject 16 has no walk<->run transition clip. Thresholds are set just above the
# best D so the graph CONNECTS (usable); the §6 source-range restriction (ON by
# default; --no-restrict-source-range for legacy all-or-nothing) keeps only the
# transition-compatible source end (fast walk -> run; fast run -> walk). These edges
# are teleport-grade, NOT clean planted transitions: the faithful fix is a bridge
# clip that CONTAINS the gait change (cf. walkToJog in the Center corpus), not tuning.
edge walk_cmu run_cmu
edge_phase_range walk_cmu run_cmu 0.60 0.95 0.05 0.40
edge_config walk_cmu run_cmu 2750 3100 4 6 41

edge run_cmu walk_cmu
edge_phase_range run_cmu walk_cmu 0.60 0.95 0.05 0.40
edge_config run_cmu walk_cmu 1950 2900 4 6 41
